  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ENV: Scaling Sustainability and Resilience of Community Conservancies in Northern Rangelands and Coastal Ecosystems of Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Kenya):  USAID will utilize FY 2022 funds in the implementation of the Scaling Sustainability and Resilience of Community Conservancies in Northern Rangelands and Coastal Ecosystems of Kenya activity the goal of which is to contribute to building the resilience of communities, ecosystems and institutions in northern and coastal Kenya to reduce the vulnerability to environmental &amp; climatic, economic and socio-political shocks.  The activity will improve the ecological health of community-owned conservation areas; support holistic rangelands, forests, wildlife, water and marine resources management; and improve pastoral and tourism-based livelihoods.  The activity will use digital ecological monitoring to collect, analyze and interpret data in real time to support decision-making and ecosystem-based adaptation approaches to protect endangered wildlife species and fragile habitats and enable them to adapt to and mitigate against climate risks. .The activity will enhance the well-being of people, livelihoods, and economy by securing community land rights--including women landowners in accordance with the Kenya&apos;s  Community Land Act (2016)--; promote peaceful co-existence amongst different ethnic communities; and mitigate human-wildlife conflict.  The goal is to expand economic opportunities for women and youth through increased entrepreneurial skills for nature-based enterprises in partnership with the private sector.  To that end, the activity will promote private-sector led market-based approaches and investments in livestock, tourism, carbon, water, renewable energy within the conservancies.  Finally, the activity will conduct institutional capacity strengthening of local conservation organizations including their governance, financial sustainability, and ability to engage in strategic partnerships with state and non-state actors to leverage private and public resources...... .. .. ..</narrative>
  </description>
